# Requirements (hypotheses)

### H1: Each channel held constant, alone

WHEN one channel is held at +1 for the whole trial and the other four are 0, THE system SHALL move the body by a distance that depends on the channel, and with all channels at 0 THE system SHALL stay near the start.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [-0.1, 0.1]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
ch = 5
lvl = 1

[[prediction]]
id = "P2"
measurement = "x"
range = [-2.0, 2.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
ch = 0
lvl = 1
```

Notes: first look, wide ranges because nothing is known. P1 is the no-drive baseline (ch = 5 means no channel driven).

### H2: A 1 Hz sine on one channel can move the body

WHEN channel c1 alone carries a 1 Hz sine of amplitude 1, THE system SHALL move the body forward by more than 0.05 m, and WHEN all five channels carry the same in-phase sine THE system SHALL stay within 0.02 m of the start.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.05, 3.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
ch = 1
f = 1.0

[[prediction]]
id = "P2"
measurement = "x"
range = [-0.02, 0.02]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
ch = 5
f = 1.0
```

Notes: ch = 0..4 drives one channel; ch = 5 drives all five with the same sine. Guess based on E1, where constants did not translate the body.

### H3: A constant on c0 amplifies the response to a sine on another channel

WHEN c0 is held at +1 and c2 carries a 1 Hz sine, THE system SHALL turn by more than 40 deg, and WHEN c1 is held at +1 instead THE system SHALL turn by less than 40 deg.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "heading"
range = [40.0, 180.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
ch = 2
g = 1

[[prediction]]
id = "P2"
measurement = "heading"
range = [-40.0, 40.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
ch = 2
g = 2
```

Notes: ch in {2,3,4} picks the sine channel (1 Hz, amplitude 1). g = 1 holds c0 at +1 and c1 at 0. g = 2 holds c1 at +1 and c0 at 0. Motivation: in E2, all channels in phase turned the body 117 deg, far more than the single-channel sum, while c0 and c1 alone did nothing.

### H4: Combined sines drive the strong turn seen with all channels in phase

WHEN c2, c3 and c4 carry the same in-phase 1 Hz sine and c0, c1 are 0, THE system SHALL turn by more than 60 deg, and WHEN only c0 and c1 carry the sine THE system SHALL stay within 5 deg of the start heading.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "heading"
range = [60.0, 180.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
set = 5

[[prediction]]
id = "P2"
measurement = "heading"
range = [-5.0, 5.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
set = 1
```

Notes: set picks which channels carry sin(2 pi t): 1 = c0,c1; 2 = c2,c3; 3 = c2,c4; 4 = c3,c4; 5 = c2,c3,c4; 6 = c0,c1,c2.
